    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0598" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg478"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 338.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to make known to
                    you formally the arrangements which have been perfected for the reception of His
                    Serene Highness Prince Louis of Battenberg, admiral of His Majesty’s second
                    cruiser squadron, and his staff during their visit to Washington as guests of
                    the government.</p>
                <p>The admiral and his staff will be brought to Washington on a special train, which
                    will leave Annapolis about 10 o’clock on the morning of Friday, November 3. At 3
                    o’clock in the afternoon of the same day they will be received by the President
                    at the White House. It is the President’s expectation that the staff of His
                    Majesty’s embassy will attend your excellency on this occasion. On Saturday, the
                    4th proximo, at 8 o’clock in the evening, it will be the President’s pleasure to
                    entertain the admiral and his staff at dinner.</p>
                <p>From the time they reach Washington until their departure from the city the
                    official responsibility of the Navy Department will be superseded by that of the
                    Department of State.</p>
                <p>They will be returned to Annapolis on the special train which brought them over,
                    but the hour of its departure has not yet been definitely determined.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
